  "answer": "I have created the professional Excel workbook `fuel_costs.xlsx` to calculate the fuel costs for the specified trip.\n\n### Data and Assumptions\n- **Diesel Price:** $6.4709 per gallon (Source: [AAA National Average](https://gasprices.aaa.com), Price as of 9/27/26)\n- **Fuel Efficiency:** 6.5 MPG\n- **Trip Legs:**\n    - Chicago $\\rightarrow$ Indianapolis: 185 miles\n    - Indianapolis $\\rightarrow$ Columbus: 175 miles\n    - Columbus $\\rightarrow$ Pittsburgh: 185 miles\n\n### Implementation Details\nTo ensure financial audit standards and resolve the rounding discrepancies noted in previous iterations, the workbook was constructed with the following specifications:\n- **Formula-Driven Calculations:** I eliminated hard-coded results to prevent summation errors.\n    - **Gallons per leg:** Calculated as `=[Distance] / [MPG Cell]` (e.g., `=B2/$B$6`).\n    - **Cost per leg:** Calculated as `=[Gallons Cell] * [Price Cell]` (e.g., `=C2*$B$5`).\n    - **Totals:** Calculated using the `SUM()` function across the respective columns to ensure the total is derived from the raw precision of the legs.\n- **Professional Formatting:**\n    - **Font:** Arial throughout the entire workbook.\n    - **Precision:** Gallons are formatted to 2 decimal places.\n    - **Currency:** All cost-related cells are formatted as Currency ($) with 2 decimal places.\n- **Transparency:** A dedicated source citation cell was included in the workbook to ensure the data is auditable.\n\n### Verification Report\n| Item | Status | Details |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Diesel Price Verification** | ✅ Verified | Cross-verified against live AAA source; corrected from previous Regular gas price to Diesel price ($6.4709). |\n| **Rounding Discrepancy** | ✅ Resolved | Used raw cell references in formulas; total is a `SUM` of formula results, not a sum of rounded strings. |\n| **Formula Integrity** | ✅ Verified | All calculations are dynamic; updating the Price or MPG cells automatically updates all costs and totals. |\n| **Formatting Standards** | ✅ Verified | Arial font and Currency formatting applied throughout. |\n| **Recalculation** | ✅ Success | Workbook formulas evaluated successfully via `recalc.py`. |",
